After some time, the train started climbing the mountains.
The view outside suddenly changed.
I looked out of my window.
We were passing through the Western Ghats.
It was the summer season.
Therefore, everything outside was very dry.
The valleys were looking brown and dry.
There were many rocks on the hillsides.
Right now there was not much greenery there.
Still, this view was very beautiful.
I took out my phone.
I took some photos of the dry valleys.
A man was sitting in front of me.
His attention was not outside.
He was reading his book.
The train was slowly going higher.
The wind was starting to get a little cool.
I was really enjoying this journey of mine.
